{"Hello! I am Bobo. Let's read a story together!":"3eb87517f885bc94.mp3","Hello! I am Nibbles. Let's read a story together!":"8d9288ed355d5065.mp3","Hello! I am Pip. Let's read a story together!":"436f1e8f22b0a965.mp3","Hello! I am Bruno. Let's read a story together!":"aa2bd6c2a5e3fb4c.mp3","Hello! I am Honey. Let's read a story together!":"ff681d9aa8bb8a6e.mp3","Hello! I am Tumble. Let's read a story together!":"c82ef0cbbcd2369a.mp3","Hello! I am Ducky. Let's read a story together!":"c8479897cdd9dcaa.mp3","Hello! I am Splash. Let's read a story together!":"0bc0353af9b86c91.mp3","Hello! I am Momo. Let's read a story together!":"26beb5505184b4ce.mp3","Hello! I am Mimi. Let's read a story together!":"bdc966958d6c0a0f.mp3","Hello! I am Pounce. Let's read a story together!":"efb98c05b3e1c755.mp3","Hello! I am Whiskers. Let's read a story together!":"a3d1c8aa23a99ae5.mp3","I don't know many words yet. Will you help me learn them?":"73774363c0e57061.mp3","Once upon a time, there were three little pigs.":"9a1f1aa4c1cf837f.mp3","The first little pig built his house out of straw.":"b358ec0d3572c300.mp3","The second little pig built his house out of sticks.":"c37cd5365874ea82.mp3","And the third little pig built his house out of strong red bricks.":"f96786a83e5b4467.mp3","But then, along came a big bad wolf!":"25b92ea16e78b99f.mp3","The wolf knocked on the door. Little pig, little pig, let me come in!":"c4d7e6c0c603c030.mp3","Not by the hair of my chinny chin chin!":"b1105ff675d7bbb6.mp3","Then I'll huff, and I'll puff, and I'll blow your house down! Blow with me! Blow into the phone!":"57619c960a78005c.mp3","Whooosh! You did it! The straw house blew away!":"509ec24a27388124.mp3","Whooosh! And the straw house blew away!":"caeb47a9b6d6f8e8.mp3","The first little pig ran to the house made of sticks!":"1d01fea033a8adda.mp3","But the wolf huffed, and he puffed, and he blew that house down too!":"2be9677379b236a4.mp3","So both little pigs ran to the house made of bricks.":"6be63261a06daf8e.mp3","The wolf huffed. And he puffed. And he huffed and he puffed.":"c14821d197d16309.mp3","But the brick house did not fall down. Bricks are too strong!":"c3021fb906542c4a.mp3","So the sneaky wolf climbed up onto the roof, and down the chimney!":"46a0b4471c866a70.mp3","But the clever little pigs had something waiting for him.":"980dc1be8341c3d2.mp3","Splash! Right into the big hot pot!":"4deee7bab09b8039.mp3","The wolf jumped up, ran out of the door, and never ever came back!":"e9828c7cc3f33cf6.mp3","And the three little pigs lived happily ever after. The end!":"443fc29d47cbb51c.mp3","Look how many words you taught me! Thank you!":"8e6e4e267f9c3b06.mp3","Ooh! What is that?":"9269efa883d4ae14.mp3","You said it! Thank you for teaching me!":"26dc2de27a35a2c7.mp3","It's a little pig!":"442b025c583d60f2.mp3","That was a pig. I will remember!":"d2cac294568482a9.mp3","Your turn! Can you say pig?":"1c27b196a8b7be40.mp3","In Spanish, we say el cerdito.":"1b22b433622e1937.mp3","pig":"ecd23d3fad020192.mp3","In Spanish, el cerdito":"04f1f73ad8524c0d.mp3","That house is made of straw.":"187a52f5847ea7cd.mp3","Straw. I will remember that!":"6244fdf0ea38e37e.mp3","Your turn! Can you say straw?":"3cc330c3ef68433b.mp3","In Spanish, we say la paja.":"527b69f7356c653a.mp3","straw":"ba06d2c0f1f5c537.mp3","In Spanish, la paja":"273bde64cf60c379.mp3","That house is made of sticks.":"6e5c6c59dc249d6a.mp3","Sticks. I will remember that!":"72479324e4684c00.mp3","Your turn! Can you say sticks?":"9c53ca175e79b6c3.mp3","In Spanish, we say los palos.":"6c93fe37222e1aa9.mp3","sticks":"60b8be8abdf98330.mp3","In Spanish, los palos":"4bf3eeacce63feaf.mp3","That house is made of strong bricks.":"263dfed1a19ce816.mp3","Bricks. I will remember that!":"c96ca64acb1bed3d.mp3","Your turn! Can you say bricks?":"ff28a9348b48d29c.mp3","In Spanish, we say los ladrillos.":"c646f56d464ca311.mp3","bricks":"034c42a9bc851839.mp3","In Spanish, los ladrillos":"10a3bdf230b716ca.mp3","It's a big bad wolf!":"24c2ac9c220fac62.mp3","That was a wolf. I will remember!":"deb85704d2dab86c.mp3","Your turn! Can you say wolf?":"033900dd2d64c5e6.mp3","In Spanish, we say el lobo.":"3b8e61d517a54756.mp3","wolf":"82c9eb80a2049fa7.mp3","In Spanish, el lobo":"0ff50748ecf17bd7.mp3","That is the chimney, on top of the roof.":"51f4d9f269226ef9.mp3","A chimney. I will remember that!":"b57e47aa07875c5b.mp3","Your turn! Can you say chimney?":"f3bcf746d32703bc.mp3","In Spanish, we say la chimenea.":"121372cc574d9de6.mp3","chimney":"f463ec81e660131a.mp3","In Spanish, la chimenea":"9758ad28f7e723b3.mp3","It's a big hot pot!":"c121dbea4a22e782.mp3","A pot. I will remember that!":"dd8857b98b57fc58.mp3","Your turn! Can you say pot?":"ce204fe9dedbaa98.mp3","In Spanish, we say la olla.":"391a232c97d2d262.mp3","pot":"2860488bc592a40c.mp3","In Spanish, la olla":"a5781d668ad2311b.mp3","Who wants to come with you today?":"e5c943cf414d9d49.mp3","Hooray! My name is Bobo!":"3bb60f5574c2fb34.mp3","Hooray! My name is Nibbles!":"4b2cdcd314c96bd4.mp3","Hooray! My name is Pip!":"3edcab4f98994e72.mp3","Hooray! My name is Bruno!":"8d9cec03d006af41.mp3","Hooray! My name is Honey!":"bee52667dda13ed6.mp3","Hooray! My name is Tumble!":"8d753941d25edd8c.mp3","Hooray! My name is Ducky!":"5753364313a7e58e.mp3","Hooray! My name is Splash!":"bd3fd0652c23c334.mp3","Hooray! My name is Momo!":"e7a30d885c46a83e.mp3","Hooray! My name is Mimi!":"482f99f9b515b0cb.mp3","Hooray! My name is Pounce!":"9cdf898fc41239ff.mp3","Hooray! My name is Whiskers!":"7f533191247cd459.mp3","What shall we call your bunny?":"fdf4cac73f10a4d4.mp3","What shall we call your bear?":"705d032f5fc00c5a.mp3","What shall we call your duck?":"182c38a76e968ca7.mp3","What shall we call your cat?":"d7c7037e874c5c00.mp3","Hello again! This one is my favourite. Will you help me learn?":"b6e5a3492c26ed16.mp3","In a sunny little garden, there lived an itsy bitsy spider.":"830c5ea1ab0fbc13.mp3","Beside the wall stood a tall metal water spout.":"dee0980496e261b9.mp3","The itsy bitsy spider wanted to climb all the way to the top.":"ba71370e3978a1c5.mp3","The itsy bitsy spider climbed up the water spout.":"c75c821042ec0583.mp3","But high above, the sky began to fill with big grey clouds.":"4a2c1b105f1ede37.mp3","Down came the rain, and washed the spider out!":"af5d64024a7614c5.mp3","Poor itsy bitsy spider. She was all the way back down, and very very wet.":"585dacac786bd81d.mp3","Can you help? Blow the rain clouds away! Blow into the phone!":"6d67412f3ff1d051.mp3","You did it! The clouds went whooshing away!":"bc698fc763675572.mp3","And slowly, the clouds went whooshing away.":"f53e01e6dfbb47da.mp3","Out came the sun, and dried up all the rain!":"6c3c2e0f4f31c599.mp3","The spider shook herself off. She was warm and dry again.":"f3fe3d3c9a167102.mp3","And the itsy bitsy spider climbed up the spout again!":"94f049a8eefc2b01.mp3","Up and up and up, all the way to the very top!":"f55f08897167f8d7.mp3","And there, in the sunshine, she made a beautiful silver web.":"4415f59411c5b1c9.mp3","The itsy bitsy spider never ever gave up. The end!":"e029d9f9e371a7a7.mp3","You taught me so many words today! Thank you!":"56b80b96cf3daf04.mp3","That's a little spider!":"3fe89b43c5d3c1ef.mp3","A spider. I will remember that!":"d721e6bef0330735.mp3","Your turn! Can you say spider?":"fd1d2a38cbcd438c.mp3","In Spanish, we say la araña.":"eb4f046e55923cbb.mp3","spider":"8967be742541226e.mp3","In Spanish, la araña":"b4f4f6cb94b18277.mp3","That is the water spout, a big metal pipe.":"095648b2e839fd78.mp3","A spout. I will remember that!":"e2f4c503c5694e94.mp3","Your turn! Can you say spout?":"0da90bce1df32ab4.mp3","In Spanish, we say el canalón.":"6df77a472a855ffc.mp3","spout":"6d683555ea1fba4d.mp3","In Spanish, el canalón":"481af242b62cd37b.mp3","She is going up, up, up!":"9a462184f7d39ef8.mp3","Up. I will remember that!":"1e29581fcce61089.mp3","Your turn! Can you say up?":"63c75774efab7b6d.mp3","In Spanish, we say arriba.":"9a2662a71b6328e9.mp3","up":"753ae0eaa5bc4bae.mp3","In Spanish, arriba":"97a8c313dc8193de.mp3","That's a big grey rain cloud.":"c390c27e94e3569b.mp3","A cloud. I will remember that!":"126d93f6de45b4cf.mp3","Your turn! Can you say cloud?":"ff47ec498dbfbf63.mp3","In Spanish, we say la nube.":"955d087a05e0f5f4.mp3","cloud":"5f7d143ae25de2aa.mp3","In Spanish, la nube":"afac35817a1bf886.mp3","That's the rain, falling down.":"6780caafb7e3c78e.mp3","Rain. I will remember that!":"9533106e32548fed.mp3","Your turn! Can you say rain?":"68b974fbb97e55f0.mp3","In Spanish, we say la lluvia.":"cd28cb31d18f1756.mp3","rain":"2e858e89f50bb1e4.mp3","In Spanish, la lluvia":"4da4f95bc53497b9.mp3","Oh no, she washed all the way down!":"a5d16c91482e2744.mp3","Down. I will remember that!":"dd739489d0fc4f38.mp3","Your turn! Can you say down?":"b5d77bd56d622160.mp3","In Spanish, we say abajo.":"a5051bbab2816371.mp3","down":"9354b9299d3ff3cd.mp3","In Spanish, abajo":"221fe811e5901294.mp3","Here comes the warm yellow sun!":"d85f3362d50d4d54.mp3","The sun. I will remember that!":"801b270b3be4d36b.mp3","Your turn! Can you say sun?":"85d5a6f42efa5957.mp3","In Spanish, we say el sol.":"9b281b04e1e9c5cd.mp3","sun":"89b5a5d70e124d60.mp3","In Spanish, el sol":"df5fa17cbe6c5a3f.mp3","She made a beautiful spider web.":"427d17330c3114e1.mp3","A web. I will remember that!":"4e0db59ea5270e8f.mp3","Your turn! Can you say web?":"dbff7575f63be474.mp3","In Spanish, we say la telaraña.":"9bafea891198648b.mp3","web":"cd102b4c0d5e8d91.mp3","In Spanish, la telaraña":"ff45ce45e61c9be2.mp3","Look, a rainbow in the sky!":"f6b57396b6c9071b.mp3","A rainbow. I will remember that!":"dc4a1e46ac0ca526.mp3","Your turn! Can you say rainbow?":"50931d89089b74f5.mp3","In Spanish, we say el arcoíris.":"1f2021f6fc281c65.mp3","rainbow":"67e1c8a1b6c25063.mp3","In Spanish, el arcoíris":"47d2f10bd2af596a.mp3","Ooh, this one is a chase! Come on, let's watch.":"d6d13e09327e2714.mp3","One sunny morning, a kind old woman was baking in her little kitchen.":"f21dd82dae22dab3.mp3","She rolled the dough flat, and cut out a little gingerbread man.":"668be5ff799b8eaa.mp3","Then she popped him into the warm oven to bake.":"8b9a76735858edae.mp3","She waited, and she waited. And then something wonderful happened.":"7174225113cc55af.mp3","Out jumped the gingerbread man! He was alive!":"eff86bb0aea8adff.mp3","And away he ran, straight out of the door.":"da10b6df92eaeeaf.mp3","Run, run, as fast as you can! You can't catch me, I'm the Gingerbread Man!":"a2f146b355451f90.mp3","He raced down the garden path, past all the flowers.":"d16ede6241febe52.mp3","He raced along the winding country lane.":"5b7f3155ab972de5.mp3","He ran past a big spotty cow, munching in the meadow.":"a064c57981801db5.mp3","Stop, little cake! said the cow. But the gingerbread man just laughed.":"08d036a3cf853bf4.mp3","He ran past a tall brown horse, standing by the golden field.":"abded932e7d44354.mp3","Stop, little cake! said the horse. But he was already gone.":"407cb3f0c448fc12.mp3","The farmers came running out of the barn to catch him.":"36b49360eb51ae42.mp3","But nobody could catch him. He was much too fast!":"0526f5c3a51fed6d.mp3","Over the green hill he went, laughing all the way.":"afb8c3774d9a02c0.mp3","Until at last, he came to a wide blue river.":"378b6d4954610243.mp3","Oh no. Gingerbread men are not very good at swimming.":"22a144a96e6ead66.mp3","Just then, a clever orange fox came padding out of the reeds.":"6d4bcc54cfc6cdd8.mp3","Hop onto my back, said the fox, and I will carry you across.":"0f5c7efc83835478.mp3","So the gingerbread man hopped on, and the fox swam into the river.":"d9e86ff8fe49b620.mp3","Halfway across, the sly fox began to tip his nose up, up, up.":"902ef410498ad582.mp3","But the gingerbread man was quick! He jumped, and landed safe on the grass.":"6cddf3bcb2e528e6.mp3","And he ran, all the way home, to the kind old woman.":"b7332ba09f174104.mp3","She laughed and laughed, and gave him the biggest hug. The end!":"7370504039dbb178.mp3","That was the best one yet! And look how many words we found.":"1757b1738387c757.mp3","oven":"e62386afc99f82e6.mp3","In Spanish, el horno":"6c235932937e7a48.mp3","run":"b7291322f48ef1c7.mp3","In Spanish, correr":"7651ac7dc5e657ac.mp3","cow":"be2b2d2689cb482f.mp3","In Spanish, la vaca":"82d898ec849c02c0.mp3","horse":"7f807c2b73935995.mp3","In Spanish, el caballo":"95fde27de159d7ce.mp3","fast":"0478d0cc25014af6.mp3","In Spanish, rápido":"8ad9d711b2f07e83.mp3","river":"1dd2f27a9ecc622a.mp3","In Spanish, el río":"4ed16cfab6cd2f17.mp3","fox":"9fa982a00794ee54.mp3","In Spanish, el zorro":"cc31b0108cfec859.mp3","home":"38b0f23d680a4765.mp3","In Spanish, la casa":"51c9770939d09b55.mp3","Say it with me. run!":"e5c4a9c95393870c.mp3","Yes! run!":"f7260bf0bafa6502.mp3","run!":"77209054de66837a.mp3","Say it with me. cow!":"d53d9de415c01fa6.mp3","Yes! cow!":"d6d5203c7f4e9925.mp3","cow!":"5dedee4100fc8ca8.mp3","Say it with me. fox!":"8e0c59add64d04b2.mp3","Yes! fox!":"00473831434e01da.mp3","fox!":"775d1db9b7611e86.mp3","Ooh, this one is a dream! Come and watch it with me.":"8f7294510d3ec4e0.mp3","On a warm summer afternoon, Alice sat by the river, feeling very sleepy.":"b6c2bd6775a96efc.mp3","When all at once, a white rabbit in a red coat came hurrying by!":"605f1d95c2328026.mp3","Oh my ears and whiskers! I'm late, I'm late, I'm terribly late!":"d4aec20ae4dda704.mp3","Alice jumped up and ran after him, through the long summer grass.":"374c8bf37f5367a8.mp3","The rabbit popped straight down a great round hole, under the hedge.":"f31685849955a976.mp3","And Alice tumbled in after him. Down, and down, and down she went.":"363ff0f1e67c6760.mp3","She floated past teacups, and ticking clocks, and old picture books, all drifting in the air.":"fc4b23fb6781d99f.mp3","Bump! Alice landed softly at the bottom, in a long hall full of little doors.":"3f3f30c890c49db2.mp3","And there on a glass table, she found a tiny golden key.":"0b905bfd54e0a8a2.mp3","It opened the very smallest door of all. And behind it was the loveliest garden.":"685992fc118f2b6a.mp3","But the door was far too little. Then Alice saw a bottle. Drink me, said the label.":"8e91a306dad4c7b3.mp3","She took one sip, and whoosh! Alice shrank until she was as small as a mouse.":"1c80e921b53c6bc1.mp3","Then she nibbled a little cake, and up she grew, big and tall, all the way to the ceiling!":"79cf19d3ee34a964.mp3","At last Alice found her way out, into a garden of enormous talking flowers.":"85c323bf868016d4.mp3","And high in a tree sat a cat, with the widest smile she had ever seen.":"50e2ed756ca989ad.mp3","We are all a little silly here. But don't you worry. You will find your way.":"7134522bf3dae46f.mp3","Then slowly, slowly, the cat faded away, until only his smile was left behind.":"f0967ec5e5354ea1.mp3","Further along the path, the Mad Hatter and the March Hare were having a tea party.":"2f702c35caf5a81f.mp3","A very merry unbirthday to you! Have a cup, have a cake, have everything!":"68c030ae11415c46.mp3","Then the trumpets sounded. It was the Queen of Hearts, marching through her roses.":"4707ff958fa5382a.mp3","Everybody up! Off you go, off you go, at once!":"6948e46a51a33c7c.mp3","But her soldiers were only playing cards! Up they flew into the sky, like confetti.":"4cc8fa56a63ee453.mp3","And Alice opened her eyes. She was back by the river, warm and safe in the sunshine.":"5025b6738f65fa0c.mp3","What a very curious dream, she said with a smile. The end!":"5ce7f30ac4a276b7.mp3","That was the best dream ever. Look at all the words we found!":"3f44efff205a07d2.mp3","Say it with me. rabbit!":"11fa4d20f103e1b1.mp3","Yes! rabbit!":"d4ebf3b251c5bd49.mp3","rabbit!":"f1d8c6eba848fa96.mp3","rabbit":"ca1788766c10beec.mp3","In Spanish, el conejo":"9f861e813cbc3c98.mp3","hole":"bacc9960b1331632.mp3","In Spanish, el agujero":"070a30cbfea52b37.mp3","key":"6295d26705399076.mp3","In Spanish, la llave":"daff87b5d0e69d70.mp3","small":"0f875131c2102e16.mp3","In Spanish, pequeño":"b6ea687d40b1903b.mp3","big":"4944b1d00c0a9fcf.mp3","In Spanish, grande":"49356734cb59f48a.mp3","Say it with me. cat!":"c01aec5ab9a73848.mp3","Yes! cat!":"c7c3d9c69904ecff.mp3","cat!":"7e06cdccfbc14175.mp3","cat":"bee265a3cad932b8.mp3","In Spanish, el gato":"c7d5e18c7a33dae3.mp3","tea":"9dd5c0502783a388.mp3","In Spanish, el té":"8c95b6444d6b2549.mp3","Say it with me. queen!":"6e1b58610106e081.mp3","Yes! queen!":"deaf6e575b38632e.mp3","queen!":"1aa1ac08b606f4a1.mp3","queen":"e43f583946f30689.mp3","In Spanish, la reina":"9a3970e543c310a1.mp3","[warmly] This one is my favourite. It is a little bit sad at the start... [brightly] but wait until the end!":"d8fad2d65785807f.mp3","[gently] Down among the tall green reeds, a mother duck sat waiting on her nest.":"632a9e0c751eca6f.mp3","[excited] Crack! Crack! Out came three tiny yellow ducklings, all fluffy and new.":"89058d68421c285d.mp3","[curiously] But the very last egg was much bigger. And out came a duckling with soft grey feathers.":"53911ebcaca50e42.mp3","[kindly] Oh! You are not yellow like the others. But you are mine, and I love you.":"fc4960e0515940f8.mp3","[warmly] The next morning, mother duck led them all down to the pond for their very first swim.":"5803e755e45ad28a.mp3","[cheerfully] Splash! The little grey one could swim beautifully. Better than all of them!":"f06ee48861e9fc09.mp3","[sadly] But the hens and the geese in the farmyard turned their backs on him.":"42ba8dcc2bffa2ac.mp3","[sadly] Why does nobody want to play with me? [quietly] Nobody at all.":"66d25a7d7663a82d.mp3","[softly] And so, as the sun went down, the little duckling felt very lonely indeed.":"0b5290e642a88c15.mp3","[gently] He walked away, far across the marshes, as the leaves turned gold and red.":"49e7deda5064c6db.mp3","[wistfully] High above him, the wild geese called to one another and flew away south.":"484d3d53882e52a9.mp3","[softly] When the rain came, he hid underneath a great green leaf, and waited.":"b2ec33aad24d2fde.mp3","[quietly] At night he saw a warm little window glowing in the dark, and he wished he had a home.":"4202a24f591d1ab8.mp3","[gently] Then the days grew colder and colder, and winter came to the marshes.":"cf0f558b7d9930fe.mp3","[carefully] The pond turned to hard shining ice, and the world went very quiet.":"c53776fadcf343b8.mp3","[warmly] A kind farmer found him shivering, and carried him into a barn full of warm straw.":"49d1437b27d3a0f8.mp3","[softly] And under all the winter stars, the little duckling slept, and waited, and grew.":"e5c426c1e39a14dc.mp3","[brightly] Then one morning the snow began to melt. The blossom opened. Spring had come at last!":"3e536b90269f5539.mp3","[wonder] And there on the water were three of the most beautiful birds he had ever seen.":"7e2b8879772d8009.mp3","[nervously] Oh, they are so lovely. They will never want me.":"e669d5568daae863.mp3","[gently] But as he came closer, he looked down into the still clear water.":"5c406f9c012614ea.mp3","[amazed] And there in the water was no grey duckling at all. There was a swan!":"fe16e2ac0df94c38.mp3","[warmly] He had been a swan all along. He was simply not grown up yet.":"8dbfd762d0d068b3.mp3","[joyfully] The three great swans curved their necks and welcomed him. You are one of us!":"b4344f3d27db2f04.mp3","[joyfully] And the children on the bank clapped their hands and said, look, that one is the most beautiful of all!":"99ee23e08821b827.mp3","[warmly] He was beautiful the whole time. He just had to grow. [brightly] Look at all our new words!":"de03eae900c23b7b.mp3","Say it with me. feather!":"ada1ea434ca2d57a.mp3","Yes! feather!":"eb05fbf966dd26f7.mp3","feather!":"1278dd2622249259.mp3","Say it with me. winter!":"0da5518c27ff5c77.mp3","Yes! winter!":"221bda2e797e01ea.mp3","winter!":"1cea0ce420d592b5.mp3","Say it with me. swan!":"b1226baa0f8c834a.mp3","Yes! swan!":"3449f44f08173811.mp3","swan!":"041cf0bf048fe429.mp3","feather":"6d73313b61347435.mp3","In Spanish, la pluma":"21f70e259733dbb1.mp3","pond":"3e81acbebf50c016.mp3","In Spanish, el estanque":"db8665f46c566e24.mp3","lonely":"fa8a4d608b9ef06c.mp3","In Spanish, solo":"e2f5fd57fa4cc8db.mp3","winter":"9c52746ee0688033.mp3","In Spanish, el invierno":"0a4414b0ca1388cf.mp3","ice":"64ff727504a9fc23.mp3","In Spanish, el hielo":"64cde5fd4d31e320.mp3","spring":"5b38b854668f3f82.mp3","In Spanish, la primavera":"599ddd7e914cd3fb.mp3","swan":"1cd888e8b4b82b1b.mp3","In Spanish, el cisne":"078432af3ae1c0d2.mp3","beautiful":"c1ec48d5503219d7.mp3","In Spanish, hermoso":"3c9c0e3a1d3cd9c4.mp3","[warmly] Ooh, this one is a big adventure. Come with me!":"ee481c3418415881.mp3","[gently] Long ago, in a village between the green mountains, there lived a kind old woman and a kind old man.":"6fdedc8c9e2aefcd.mp3","[warmly] Every morning, she went down to the sparkling river to wash the clothes.":"9212c8b042b1594c.mp3","[amazed] When one day, bobbing along on the water, came the biggest peach she had ever seen!":"15e638b75fc26d6f.mp3","[cheerfully] So the two of them carried it home together, all the way up the hill.":"a7a00b6d9c8ed8be.mp3","[excited] And when it opened — crack! — inside sat a laughing baby boy!":"2584233be7c9d831.mp3","[joyfully] Then we shall call you Momotaro. Our own little peach boy!":"a04e4e4746fed422.mp3","[warmly] Momotaro grew up strong and kind, and helped them both every single day.":"68ad6ee2c051ff9e.mp3","[gently] Until one morning, he stood up tall. He had made up his mind to be brave.":"5ea19d42b7804c16.mp3","[boldly] I am big and strong now. I will sail to the island, and ask the giants to give back everything they took.":"28dc99b0a5c6851f.mp3","[kindly] Then take these millet dumplings, the very best in all Japan. You will need them on your journey.":"57f350025e9f0ed6.mp3","[warmly] And so, with a bundle tied to a stick, Momotaro set off.":"e5a393957d31ae3c.mp3","[gently] His path wound up and up, through the pine trees and the mountain mist.":"9f4b099221a7b090.mp3","[curiously] And there on the path sat a dog, sniffing the air and wagging his tail. Would he like to be a friend?":"0eac0974efe2463c.mp3","[eagerly] Ooh, that smells wonderful! Give me one dumpling and I will come with you!":"1de36cf45f2f4ea5.mp3","[playfully] Next, a cheeky monkey came swinging down out of the branches.":"27e7437683fbba9b.mp3","[cheekily] Me too, me too! I am very good at climbing things!":"d336c32a6001e8b9.mp3","[brightly] And last of all, a pheasant swooped down in a flash of red and green.":"2bc1cdba7a663379.mp3","[warmly] Now there were four of them. And nobody felt frightened any more.":"51bb8517b4d7e18a.mp3","[gently] They walked until the path ran out, and there in front of them lay the wide blue sea.":"229eea55889c8264.mp3","[excited] Into the little boat they climbed, and away they sailed across the waves!":"3f6f1d981767a300.mp3","[wonder] Until at last, rising out of the blue, came the island with its great red gate.":"89468c643778b43a.mp3","[playfully] The giants were enormous. But Momotaro put his hands on his hips, and asked them very firmly to give everything back.":"b682ac3efaec612b.mp3","[sheepishly] Oh... oh dear. We are very sorry. We did not think anybody would mind.":"52c234169d04a297.mp3","[warmly] And they handed back every last coin, and promised never to take anything again.":"9617f6ea4593a4b5.mp3","[joyfully] So home they sailed with the treasure, all the way back to the little village.":"61978b3511d8c346.mp3","[joyfully] And the old woman and the old man came running out with their arms wide open. The end!":"321683018dd9fe73.mp3","[warmly] He was brave, and he was kind. [brightly] That is the very best kind of hero. Look at all our new words!":"492b55dc97324472.mp3","Say it with me. peach!":"a1d630fc01ba59e5.mp3","Yes! peach!":"6b3e3bf3695e5467.mp3","peach!":"1a3292b3e64ae636.mp3","Say it with me. friend!":"950f83b53d65fab2.mp3","Yes! friend!":"9b0a19622b5d840f.mp3","friend!":"07580420d1f670d7.mp3","Say it with me. boat!":"28999d5a30cfc119.mp3","Yes! boat!":"b6a97cb85ab6542c.mp3","boat!":"173d6ab5dfd71947.mp3","peach":"87dd5e49ac59b15b.mp3","In Spanish, el melocotón":"cfae30432555cdba.mp3","brave":"2562c727955f978c.mp3","In Spanish, valiente":"683532951e30ebfb.mp3","journey":"e6819907228bb6ad.mp3","In Spanish, el viaje":"614b9da486fa1568.mp3","mountain":"892ca7d1c5460ee6.mp3","In Spanish, la montaña":"00af61971a9ddb6b.mp3","friend":"0c87551d53aa547f.mp3","In Spanish, el amigo":"58de84652d5996e0.mp3","boat":"b6ee5ec0f098422a.mp3","In Spanish, el barco":"6882ae23c5b7170c.mp3","island":"74b972267902f9bd.mp3","In Spanish, la isla":"b9e67d0c0575874f.mp3","treasure":"f777208dcbf142e1.mp3","In Spanish, el tesoro":"bbff91b30245af44.mp3","[warmly] Ooh, I love this one. It is all about sharing.":"a0722e21cf57e719.mp3","[gently] One evening, a traveller came walking along the road, looking for somewhere to rest.":"e8fc1c627dcf0ca3.mp3","[gently] At the top of the hill he found a little village, with a stone well in the middle of the square.":"cc5dbbf1b14351a5.mp3","[quietly] But as he arrived, every shutter clicked shut, and every door closed tight.":"2469e80c68a64cd2.mp3","[quietly] For the villagers had had a hard year, and each one hid away what little food they had.":"122eebec69844f1a.mp3","[gently] He knocked at one door. And then another. But nobody came out.":"ef40bcfbf195dc62.mp3","[softly] So the traveller sat down on the edge of the well. He was very tired, and very hungry.":"ca25e71582fedaf7.mp3","[brightly] And then... he had an idea. A really rather good idea!":"8339f6126f41813c.mp3","[cheerfully] He built a little fire in the square, and hung a great big pot of water over it.":"57c81b4cb47908ee.mp3","[wonder] Then he bent down, and picked up one smooth grey stone.":"a693d4bb812c4038.mp3","[grandly] Stone soup! Ahh. There is nothing in all the world quite like a good stone soup.":"94fc3e3a51673fbb.mp3","[playfully] And plop! In went the stone. Behind every window, somebody was watching.":"3ebfec71241dcec6.mp3","[happily] He stirred, and he hummed, and he smiled a very big smile indeed.":"ac620f9f693cebdd.mp3","[curiously] And slowly, one by one, the doors began to creak open.":"97c7a61a7ef10677.mp3","[curiously] What are you making? Can I see? Can I?":"348313609d80a7dc.mp3","[thoughtfully] Mmm. Wonderful. Although... I do think it would be even better with one carrot.":"439652aea3da6f5d.mp3","[brightly] Carrots! Oh, I have carrots. Wait right there!":"0b8bb7bf89eb78c7.mp3","[cheerfully] And then came potatoes. And onions. And cabbages, and beans, and barley.":"53c721decc5926e2.mp3","[warmly] The big pot bubbled and steamed until it was full right up to the brim.":"8fb2b594dc6f91c4.mp3","[delighted] And when at last they tasted it — oh! It was absolutely delicious.":"487d7125d63e283b.mp3","[joyfully] So out came the tables, up went the lanterns, and the whole village ate together.":"91f2f3dc96701a34.mp3","[warmly] Not one of them had had enough on their own. But together, there was plenty for everybody.":"eef1da768be28eaf.mp3","[gently] In the morning, the traveller waved goodbye. He had brought no food with him at all. He had brought something better. He had taught them how to share.":"3ebf9f16facc5096.mp3","[joyfully] And the little girl in the red coat kept that stone forever. The end!":"36533d12e7e30791.mp3","[warmly] A stone cannot really make soup. But it can make friends. [brightly] Look at all our new words!":"1d7e28aea2c9b742.mp3","Say it with me. village!":"05b72e7151c19ff6.mp3","Yes! village!":"fdc338a326af2c3d.mp3","village!":"ef99d43610ac9d86.mp3","Say it with me. stone!":"9c991e844456a98b.mp3","Yes! stone!":"22800b057c0d9b2c.mp3","stone!":"3e7a6b595005cec4.mp3","Say it with me. share!":"004505dc058a3fba.mp3","Yes! share!":"c83b8733e302d304.mp3","share!":"4fed09a0b0fa2512.mp3","village":"f57708b06895ae32.mp3","In Spanish, el pueblo":"9ec3c428fd126833.mp3","hungry":"018efc5017eb5095.mp3","In Spanish, hambriento":"e007ade9b93cb791.mp3","stone":"d1e669f094e5af1a.mp3","In Spanish, la pie